ible  you've generated a website called mini  scope org and this website users and  developers can interact all the parks  lists and designs and and and circuit  board layouts all the software is all  provided there and people can go there  and develop their own microscopes and  even make improvements to the current  microscopes there's a lot of  interactions and so I'll go into this a  little bit later but I think this is a  critical thing for the development of  this open-source resource and so what  are these microscopes in essence look  like this is the animal on the left you  can see the mouse is carrying this  microscope and the a lens which is you  can see is this you see if I can point  to it this this grin lens here which is  a cylindrical piece of glass that acts  as the focusing mechanism gets implanted  over whatever structure you'd like to  image they had the cells will already be  expressing the genetically encoded  calcium indicator that you're interested  in and later on the animal is brought  back and a base plate isn't  mounted over the head of the animal  which which holds the microscope in  place and this is adjusted with while  the microscope is on the head of the  animal to image the maximal number of  cells and eventually when the animal  needs to be imaged the the microscope  climbs onto this base plate  the cells are imaged then when you're  done the animal doesn't have to go  around with the microscope on his head  and so what what will happen is the  animal will the microscope will come off  and the animal will go back there the  great thing is the the microscope can go  back the next day or the next week and  the same exact group of animals are  imaged and the group of cells are imaged  and and this is all interactive with the  behavioral camera here you can see the  raw images that that we record and the  Delta F over F images that we've been  we've been also recording and you can  see that the signal-to-noise ratios are  quite high and 